[{:db/id "q-279125/field-1/105d4ccce6b4014e994bfa2f74d50108d2866668d615f21acb7d09db0f9d2258" :answer/id #uuid "793eab90-288c-5025-9f72-bd8efe019373" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{64}+\\frac{y^2}{20.25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-279125/field-1/2c7b677796d1e670990413810721c40786de33c276edc78440128e418fd011f3" :answer/id #uuid "f0d6fef3-08ed-5337-84c2-0832a2cd81b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{8}+\\frac{y^2}{4.5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-279125/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "de883f47-5217-5724-8d3f-ca5ad38dcdec" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-279125/field-1/105d4ccce6b4014e994bfa2f74d50108d2866668d615f21acb7d09db0f9d2258" :answer-field/choices ["q-279125/field-1/105d4ccce6b4014e994bfa2f74d50108d2866668d615f21acb7d09db0f9d2258" "q-279125/field-1/2c7b677796d1e670990413810721c40786de33c276edc78440128e418fd011f3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-279125" :question/id #uuid "a238f27d-73c6-5f1a-903f-f75b1e29e25b" :question/math-academy-id "q-279125" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039348/assets/e1bfe4335b41f14dce0f3d614ca108a4d6d83c4aa65fc44f169431175c82f1b5.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=8$ and the vertical radius has length $b=\\frac{9}{2}.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{8}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{(\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{64}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\frac{81}{4})} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{64}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{81} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-279125/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f88c1deb-cd11-5b68-b90b-2d8edfae2469"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-279125"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-279130/field-1/c51785d49fc71d97e065e8ce5ca9c5ce8a74af90d3e89f21a77c72a2ac457371" :answer/id #uuid "2aa45642-0521-51cd-b388-2f8d10af62b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{72.25}+\\frac{y^2}{12.25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-279130/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "714dfb41-290d-5d13-9fa0-9159e509b7db" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-279130/field-1/c51785d49fc71d97e065e8ce5ca9c5ce8a74af90d3e89f21a77c72a2ac457371" :answer-field/choices ["q-279130/field-1/c51785d49fc71d97e065e8ce5ca9c5ce8a74af90d3e89f21a77c72a2ac457371"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-279130" :question/id #uuid "a1361ab6-806b-56de-924f-b7e320596a4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-279130" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039348/assets/1fcd12762c7b86e1d40813a747b75e1f9b21d83787824f5f48725ac9a1dddff6.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=\\frac{17}{2}$ and the vertical radius has length $b=\\frac{7}{2}.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{(\\frac{17}{2})}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{(\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\frac{289}{4})}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\frac{49}{4})} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{289}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{49} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-279130/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f88c1deb-cd11-5b68-b90b-2d8edfae2469"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-279130"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-7604"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039348/assets/d2c35e72acad77ae747c6a78c9794e9b076c047891d4b12d5c9b3176bdc6dde5.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-73619"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039348/assets/8637901efc126236b190e7012cf65a06be078cb21c3093eff39b927493000138.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-7603"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039348/assets/8ac809353e7834d328d645fafb5c02e17386ba087e778a841865ef6313893e79.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=\\frac{7}{2}$ and the vertical radius has length $b=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3.5}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{(\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\frac{{7}^{2}}{{2}^{2}})}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\frac{49}{4})}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{49}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-115129/selection/4fb89e534c0ebf2d047ff968d0cc71fd343192d151879667505992c4bcd83a13" :answer/id #uuid "3018ea92-63a7-573e-b157-ec5f717b1254" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115129/selection/213de78df0e7437dbc5086404e858332c78a03be5abb1abf714e31df9103fb7a" :answer/id #uuid "31bd6c00-f798-5f52-8846-d0354e446d46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115129/selection/87170e19caf564492f238d84d6f519499e3e9ad593281c0e0c782ee56b66cd1d" :answer/id #uuid "3569ca0f-f09b-58e7-b673-c4e366db8821" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{1}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115129/selection/458c9a5790c4b8ec6863ba83037b2682e5be23fe900b7c9261f7e9ad4e275016" :answer/id #uuid "0f790dec-57a6-50e2-ae78-aecfd1e526bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{1}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115129/selection/584af32816ca47a6bdaf0807509651369dfdbbd6a1c770e7da10f0c22fea2e6d" :answer/id #uuid "1de88b45-c080-5a50-be90-5f0c5be697c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115129/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "12fc5801-5621-5551-975d-5ccdd051d75a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115129/selection/458c9a5790c4b8ec6863ba83037b2682e5be23fe900b7c9261f7e9ad4e275016" :answer-field/choices ["q-115129/selection/4fb89e534c0ebf2d047ff968d0cc71fd343192d151879667505992c4bcd83a13" "q-115129/